//   1. an OBSERVED vtype (a vsetvli earlier in this same translation block pinned it) -- which is
//      the case in the frozen S1.1-fix1 workload, whose every kernel has its vsetvli in-block;
//   2. no observation at all (rvv_bb_vtype == ~0u) -- then the single admitted shape is PROPOSED as
//      a candidate and the emitted guard proves it at run time, on every execution.
// A wrong candidate cannot produce a wrong answer: the guard fails and the already-verified helper
// runs -- the same helper TranslateHelper would have called, with the same raw instruction word.
//
